{"availability":"available","full":"amyrmahdy/decima","name":"decima","description":"Open, CPU-sized Jev-style (System One) decision model: situation + question + options → calibrated probabilities. 122M, ~20 ms on one CPU core, runs in your browser.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":1,"created":"2026-09-27T12:12:35Z","updated":"2026-10-08T12:16:47Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["calibration","decision-model","jev","jev-alternative","multilingual","onnx","system-one","typed-decisions","zero-shot-classification"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/amyrmahdy/decima-playground","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:43.022Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:43.022Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:43.022Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:26.156Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:29:35.217Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:07:43.022Z","stars":1,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Situation + question + your options → calibrated probabilities. Like TypeSafe's Jev, Decima is a System One model: typed decisions with probabilities instead of generated text. Unlike Jev, it is open (Apache-2.0), runs on a CPU, and speaks the same /v1/systemone API.","Built by A. M. Madani (@amyrmahdy · amyrmahdy.github.io). The name: DECIsion MAking — and Decima is also the Roman Fate who decides.","shell commands, local services, recursive deletes. Correction: part of the 130-case hand-written set had near-copies in the training data, so its 0.90 → 0.93 overstates the gain. On 40 fresh cases with no copies in training, 2.0 and 2.1 both score 0.83 (decima-base: 0.60). Training mixes now drop any row that copies a test case."],"features":["decima-agent 2.1 (v2.1) is trained on field logs: real-shape","Long questions no longer tie. When \"question + option\" ran past the 64-token choice window, the options were cut off,","D